That's how it felt. Still, we practiced hard.

290
00:22:37,880 --> 00:22:41,440
Even performing while standing still
takes quite a lot of practice.

291
00:22:41,440 --> 00:22:48,159
You don't know what to do with your hands.
— This hand, I mean. Right, right. Your hand—

292
00:22:48,159 --> 00:22:53,039
and you can't hold the mic with both hands,
and you can't put them in your pockets either.

293
00:22:53,039 --> 00:22:57,440
Right. — So, what does "deserve" mean?

294
00:22:57,440 --> 00:23:02,840
It means being worthy of doing something.
Having the right to it. In English. — Yeah, yeah.

295
00:23:02,840 --> 00:23:07,240
Wow, I honestly didn't know.
It does sound like a good meaning, though—

296
00:23:07,240 --> 00:23:09,200
It's different from "dissolve," right?
— Different. Totally different.

297
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:12,600
Right. — I thought of dessert, actually.
— Deserve, deserve.

298
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:17,635
Ah — you've worked so hard this year,
and you're in the middle of a world tour,

299
00:23:17,635 --> 00:23:20,440
